cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PolyNet, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PolyNet: A Python Package for Polymer Informatics"
type: software
version: 1.0.4
date-released: 2026-10-19
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  PolyNet is a Python package for polymer property prediction from (P)SMILES of
  homopolymers and copolymers. It trains graph neural networks and traditional
  machine-learning models on repeated train/validation/test splits, compares
  them statistically, explains their predictions (GNN fragment masking and
  SHAP), and predicts new polymers with ensembles and an applicability domain,
  through a YAML-driven command-line pipeline or a Streamlit GUI.
